# Third-party library configurations.

Each third-party dependency gets its own `.cmake` file in this directory
(e.g. `googletest.cmake`, `fmt.cmake`).

## Convention: namespaced interface targets

Every third-party library **must** be exposed as a namespaced interface-style
target (e.g. `re2::re2`, `fmt::fmt`, `GTest::gtest_main`) so consumers can
link directly:

```cmake
target_link_libraries(<target> PRIVATE re2::re2)
```

Rules for each `<lib>.cmake` file:

1. Prefer `find_package` first; fall back to `FetchContent` if not found.
2. If the library does not provide a namespaced target itself, create an
   `INTERFACE`/`IMPORTED` alias that carries include dirs and flags:

   ```cmake
   add_library(re2::re2 ALIAS re2)
   # or, for a raw found library:
   add_library(re2::re2 INTERFACE IMPORTED)
   target_include_directories(re2::re2 INTERFACE ${RE2_INCLUDE_DIRS})
   target_link_libraries(re2::re2 INTERFACE ${RE2_LIBRARIES})
   ```

3. Do not leak include directories or definitions globally — keep everything
   attached to the namespaced target.
4. Register the file in `cmake/thirdparty.cmake` with one `include(<lib>)`
   line (that file is the entry point, already on `CMAKE_MODULE_PATH`), and
   add the library to the `vcpkg.json` manifest.
